ss=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1122398#post1122398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">89 Dreams of Home would be that one that Rose was talking about that had the strange new type of Fae, I think it was some ideallic kind of town in Vermont/New Hampshire or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard a Lee is a sailing term, so you may be right on that one. Where did Rose meantioned that? <br /> <br /> There is a property known as Hard a Lee in Bermuda, but while that would be awesome, I don't think that's the setting.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for those of you who are not seafolk, hard a lee means to sail downwind, if that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 07-29-2017, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:15:12-07:00","id":1122400,"title":"","content":"\u201cHard A Lee\u201d is announced by the helmsman as they start to turn into the wind. (hard-a-lee means pushing the tiller hard to the lee side. each crew member needs to be sure they are free of line and duck beneath the boom).&quot;<br /> <br /> This is what I found when I looked up Hard a Lee, its a sailing term. So it could be Miami, that was never revealed, but I don't think so as that really doesn't fit into the original plot of Miami.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can find the origins of the term, maybe English.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:19:20-07:00","id":1122401,"title":"","content":"I went to look up Hard-a-Lee again, and one of the first suggestions to pop up when I typed in those words, before I hit enter, was Hard-a-Lee Bermuda, which seemed like it wasn't by choice so I'm guessing its a Bermuda setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:22:06-07:00","id":1122402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1122401#post1122401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went to look up Hard-a-Lee again, and one of the first suggestions to pop up when I typed in those words, before I hit enter, was Hard-a-Lee Bermuda, which seemed like it wasn't by choice so I'm guessing its a Bermuda setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. It would be cool, but from what I can see, it's the name of an estate that is currently on sale, which makes me think it is coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:23:09-07:00","id":1122404,"title":"","content":"(Hard-a-Lee, like the other ones I listed, is the name of the setting, not the name of the location it's in.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:27:51-07:00","id":1122406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1122399#post1122399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard a Lee is a sailing term, so you may be right on that one. Where did Rose meantioned that? <br /> <br /> There is a property known as Hard a Lee in Bermuda, but while that would be awesome, I don't think that's the setting.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for those of you who are not seafolk, hard a lee means to sail downwind, if that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div> You ninja'd me on the sailing term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:42:35-07:00","id":1122412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings#post1122342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I know that New Orleans and Reykjavik are in 2e, Paris is out, but Arc has released it online. Toronto, Tokyo, and Miami are still up in the air to the best of my knowledge. Am I missing anything? Anyone heard anything else? Anyone willing to give up spoilers? The Signature Settings are one of my favourite things about 2e, and I am super excited to see what happens in Iceland.</div> </div> </div> </div> From reading Arc's thread its safe guess that she made the same offer that she made to him, to those who wrote Honshu, Toronto, and Miami, it would only be logical.<br /> <br /> So unless they decided to keep if fanon, instead of canon like Arc did, which I doubt, then its a safe bet that they are still in. Plus if they had been pulled I think we'd know about it now, I don't think Rose would toy with fan expectations like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T12:44:22-07:00","id":1122432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1122412#post1122412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From reading Arc's thread its safe guess that she made the same offer that she made to him, to those who wrote Honshu, Toronto, and Miami, it would only be logical.<br /> <br /> So unless they decided to keep if fanon, instead of canon like Arc did, which I doubt, then its a safe bet that they are still in. Plus if they had been pulled I think we'd know about it now, I don't think Rose would toy with fan expectations like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's a safe assumption. Arc's project started on the forums, then got included as part of 2e. Rose may have taken that into account and offered to yield creative control back to Arc for that reason. There is no indication that she would be obliged to do so, or felt it neccesary for the settings that were originally commissioned for 2e. Paris could very well be a special situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T13:04:12-07:00","id":1122444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1122412#post1122412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From reading Arc's thread its safe guess that she made the same offer that she made to him, to those who wrote Honshu, Toronto, and Miami, it would only be logical.<br /> <br /> So unless they decided to keep if fanon, instead of canon like Arc did, which I doubt, then its a safe bet that they are still in. Plus if they had been pulled I think we'd know about it now, I don't think Rose would toy with fan expectations like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did <i>not</i> opt to keep it canon, instead opting to step back and keep it as fanon material. I could have gotten paid for it, updated it, and had it released in a future book, since the settings for the core are decided. I opted to skip the payment.<br /> <br /> Rose approached me wanting to make sure I got paid for my writing. I was the one who put forth the question of keeping it for myself should I want to release is as fanon rather than canon. Since it wasn't going to make it into the core, there was no problem with me making that choice for Rose.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to say that that means the other cities aren't in there, because I have no idea how it went for everyone else. I'm just saying that's how it went for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T13:04:56-07:00","id":1122446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1122432#post1122432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that's a safe assumption. Arc's project started on the forums, then got included as part of 2e. Rose may have taken that into account and offered to yield creative control back to Arc for that reason. There is no indication that she would be obliged to do so, or felt it neccesary for the settings that were originally commissioned for 2e. Paris could very well be a special situation.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, but I think my underling point that she seemed inclined to retain those setting still stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T13:07:36-07:00","id":1122448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1122444#post1122444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually did <i>not</i> opt to keep it canon, instead opting to step back and keep it as fanon material. I could have gotten paid for it, updated it, and had it released in a future book, since the settings for the core are decided. I opted to skip the payment.<br /> <br /> Rose approached me wanting to make sure I got paid for my writing. I was the one who put forth the question of keeping it for myself should I want to release is as fanon rather than canon. Since it wasn't going to make it into the core, there was no problem with me making that choice for Rose.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to say that that means the other cities aren't in there, because I have no idea how it went for everyone else. I'm just saying that's how it went for me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I understand, its just that I'd be surprised if she didn't approach the other writers to update their setting as well.<br /> <br /> I guess the only one who can answer that is Rose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T06:39:49-07:00","id":1122685,"title":"","content":"I would absolutely lose my shit if Hard-A-Lee was a Nova Scotian setting. It would be a long shot, but all of those pirate tropes that work so well with Changeling? Halifax can play with them all.<br /> <br /> And I'm not just saying that because I'm in Nova Scotia right now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T09:32:18-07:00","id":1122723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1122685#post1122685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would absolutely lose my shit if Hard-A-Lee was a Nova Scotian setting. It would be a long shot, but all of those pirate tropes that work so well with Changeling? Halifax can play with them all.<br /> <br /> And I'm not just saying that because I'm in Nova Scotia right now!</div> </div> </div> </div> 2 Canadian settings in one book? <br /> <br /> Well they've had multiple American settings and Canada is bigger and just as diverse so why not, as a Canadian I'd love that.<br /> <br /> My dad's a blue noser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T11:04:59-07:00","id":1124383,"title":"","content":"just to sum up: there are four settings in the CtL 2E core's settings chapter - <br /> 89 Dreams of Home<br /> the Council of Elves<br /> Hard-a-Lee<br /> Tumbledown Market (setting confirmed by dev blog as being New Orleans, with the French Quarter Market Courts system: Coins, Barter, Favors, &amp; Shady Deals)<br /> <br /> One of the remaining 3 is Reykjavik (Council of Elves is a favorite candidate earlier in this forum). Hong Kong has been mentioned in passing as well (given it's island and coastal trading history and time as a British protectorate, my money is on Hard-a-Lee, being a nautical term). that leaves one unknown location. I recall Rose mentioning Ipswich, MA, so perhaps that's the missing fourth and being coastal would also be a candidate for the Hard-a-Lee setting, though Rose mentioned that Ipswich, MA is not Changelings only, but fae people a category all their own, so the diversity would also give it a claim on 89 Dreams of Home<br /> <br /> the 2e book lines except for Demon the Descent (CoD - Hurt Locker, VtR 2e core, WtF 2e Core, MtAw 2e Core, PtC 2e Core, BtP Core, &amp; Dark Eras - so much groundwork would make it an awesome candidate for a Crossover Chronicle setting) have a Tokyo city or surrounding area around Tokyo as a setting. I'd love to see Tokyo as a post-core CtL2e setting eventually and keep the tradition going in GtS 2e, HtV 2e &amp; DtR, or perhaps see it in the Hedge and post-core books in the other lines if it can't fit in the core space. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:23:02-07:00","id":1124498,"title":"","content":"I don't think Toronto, Tokyo, and Miami are gone, I think Rose gave us four new settings. Only Rose knows for sure. Besides Miami was the signature setting for 1e, it'd, be weird if it wasn't in 2e at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:41:23-07:00","id":1124530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1124498#post1124498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Toronto, Tokyo, and Miami are gone, I think Rose gave us four new settings. Only Rose knows for sure. Besides Miami was the signature setting for 1e, it'd, be weird if it wasn't in 2e at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T18:04:12-07:00","id":1124554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1124530#post1124530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T18:05:46-07:00","id":1124555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1124383#post1124383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just to sum up: there are four settings in the CtL 2E core's settings chapter - <br /> 89 Dreams of Home<br /> the Council of Elves<br /> Hard-a-Lee<br /> Tumbledown Market (setting confirmed by dev blog as being New Orleans, with the French Quarter Market Courts system: Coins, Barter, Favors, &amp; Shady Deals)<br /> <br /> One of the remaining 3 is Reykjavik (Council of Elves is a favorite candidate earlier in this forum). Hong Kong has been mentioned in passing as well (given it's island and coastal trading history and time as a British protectorate, my money is on Hard-a-Lee, being a nautical term). that leaves one unknown location. I recall Rose mentioning Ipswich, MA, so perhaps that's the missing fourth and being coastal would also be a candidate for the Hard-a-Lee setting, though Rose mentioned that Ipswich, MA is not Changelings only, but fae people a category all their own, so the diversity would also give it a claim on 89 Dreams of Home<br /> <br /> the 2e book lines except for Demon the Descent (CoD - Hurt Locker, VtR 2e core, WtF 2e Core, MtAw 2e Core, PtC 2e Core, BtP Core, &amp; Dark Eras - so much groundwork would make it an awesome candidate for a Crossover Chronicle setting) have a Tokyo city or surrounding area around Tokyo as a setting. I'd love to see Tokyo as a post-core CtL2e setting eventually and keep the tradition going in GtS 2e, HtV 2e &amp; DtR, or perhaps see it in the Hedge and post-core books in the other lines if it can't fit in the core space. </div> </div> </div> </div> Hong Kong would be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T21:10:34-07:00","id":1124608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1124498#post1124498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Toronto, Tokyo, and Miami are gone, I think Rose gave us four new settings. Only Rose knows for sure. Besides Miami was the signature setting for 1e, it'd, be weird if it wasn't in 2e at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am disinclined to agree given how Rose said &quot;all four.&quot; I would be happy to be wrong though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T22:08:45-07:00","id":1124619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1124498#post1124498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Miami was the signature setting for 1e, it'd, be weird if it wasn't in 2e at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire had New Orleans, Werewolf the Rockies, Mage Boston. So far none of the second editions have revisited their 'signature' settings, except in some passing mentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T03:46:43-07:00","id":1124683,"title":"","content":"Dang, you right, still we know that Miami was written up, along with Honshu and Toronto, so unless the writers refused to update the settings to the new rule set, which I doubt, then they should still be in, why would Rose cut popular settings if she doesn't need too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:09:05-07:00","id":1124687,"title":"","content":"This is the reference to Ipswich your talking about. <br /> <br /> &quot;A thing that's worth keeping in mind about different kinds of faerie creatures: the boundaries are not always firm. Each of the categories we as designers/players define have strong characteristics that distinguish them, but in practice, all sorts of weird exceptions and one-off events happen. So, for example, the circumstances of changelings and fae-touched and hobogblins are distinct from each other, but transitions and half-measures could happen in actual play.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe I'll post the Ipswich, MA setting as one of the dev blogs. It nicely illustrates fae people who are a category of their own.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:23:24-07:00","id":1124689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1124687#post1124687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the reference to Ipswich your talking about.<br /> <br /> &quot;A thing that's worth keeping in mind about different kinds of faerie creatures: the boundaries are not always firm. Each of the categories we as designers/players define have strong characteristics that distinguish them, but in practice, all sorts of weird exceptions and one-off events happen. So, for example, the circumstances of changelings and fae-touched and hobogblins are distinct from each other, but transitions and half-measures could happen in actual play.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe I'll post the Ipswich, MA setting as one of the dev blogs. It nicely illustrates fae people who are a category of their own.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>yep, that's the reference. With the Tumbledown Market as an example of things to come, I'm quite excited to see Ipswich and the rest<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:48:11-07:00","id":1124695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipswich,_Massachusetts\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Ipswich%2C_Massachusetts.jpg/1280px-Ipswich%2C_Massachusetts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipswich,_Massachusetts\" target=\"_blank\"> Ipswich, Massachusetts - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipswich,_Massachusetts\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipswich,_Massachusetts </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've never heard of, Ipswich before, its calls itself the Birthplace of American Independence, it had America's, last witchtrial, alot of old archtecture, when Colonists had settled the area, much of the local FN population was gone, likely do to smallpox (sad obviously). It has a harbour, so it could Hard-A-Lee.<br /> <br /> We know its got a special kind of Fae, but nothing from its history suggests what it would be, except maybe some kind of Lovecraftian Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:51:50-07:00","id":1124697,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunwich_(Lovecraft\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunwich_(Lovecraft</a>)<br /> <br /> Ipswich might have been the inspiration for Dunwich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:45:18-07:00","id":1124713,"title":"","content":"Just a thought, but if the New Orleans Court's, trods extended beyond, America to globally, you could, use it as a connecting point between settings, making an ubar setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:56:07-07:00","id":1124718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122342-2e-signature-settings?p=1124713#post1124713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought, but if the New Orleans Court's, trods extended beyond, America to globally, you could, use it as a connecting point between settings, making an ubar setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. That was literally my first thought when I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}